 ### Fixed
+- **`ctx_edit` no longer fails on an `old_string` quoted from a compressed `ctx_read`
+  view.** Lossy modes (e.g. `aggressive`) strip blank lines and comments, halve the
+  indentation and merge closers (`}}`), so text the agent copied from the view never
+  occurred verbatim on disk and the edit failed with "old_string not found". `ctx_edit`
+  now falls back to a line-level match that skips the hidden lines and ignores
+  indentation (only when it is unambiguous), then patches only the changed lines:
+  hidden comments/blank lines and the file's real indentation are preserved, and
+  inserted lines are re-indented to the file's style.
 - **The Codex `lean-ctx -c` SessionStart hook is no longer a redundant nag (#625).**
   Codex's `PreToolUse` hook already rewrites every rewritable Bash command to
   `lean-ctx -c "<command>"` transparently (`permissionDecision: allow` +
